    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this case is decided by the waiting-time arithmetic, not by conduct. The driver genuinely arrived. The 'arrived' event is at 13:12:40, and the GPS trace puts him stationary at the pin throughout — all 25 fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, mean distance 2.32 m, maximum 3.71 m, constant 0.0 km/h — so POL-NS-02 is satisfied, limb (b) of POL-NS-01 is met on the driver's side, and I accept the driver's points that this is a real arrival at the pin and that the marker was not false: the 10 second event-to-fix offset is well inside the 90 second skew tolerance and neither POL-NS-05 trigger (over 300 m, or at or above 15 km/h) engages. But POL-NS-01 is conjunctive, and the dwell fails. Measured as POL-NS-01(c) directs — from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 13:12:50, not from the 'arrived' tap, to the rider's cancellation at 13:16:50 — the driver held position for 240 seconds against the 300 second STANDARD minimum, a 60 second shortfall. Limb (d) also fails: the trip record shows cancelled_by RIDER with status CANCELLED_BY_RIDER at 13:16:50, not a driver termination on one of the recognised reason codes. The fee is therefore not chargeable under POL-NS-01, and POL-NS-06 is decisive: where the effective in-geofence dwell is below the minimum for the zone class, the cancellation fee is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded to messages. The only way to reach 300 seconds was to sum separate in-geofence intervals under POL-NS-06(i), which requires a traffic advisory that is present and populated; EV-ADVIS-00706-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and can carry no fact, so that route is closed and the shortfall stands. The refund is the cancellation-fee line only: SGD 4.00, which is the whole contested amount and reconciles with fee_schedule (STANDARD zone-class fee 4.00 and RYDE_POOL vehicle-tier fee 4.00 — the greater is 4.00, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect)